---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';
---

<Layout title="About" description={`What ${site.name} is, who runs it, and how it is built and paid for.`}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">A small set of tools for activity files, run by one independent developer.</p>

    <h2>Why it exists</h2>
    <p>
      Fixing or joining an activity file usually means either buying desktop software for a one-off problem or
      uploading the file, with your home location in it, to someone's server. Neither is necessary. A FIT file is
      small and the work is simple enough for a browser to do on its own.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is built</h2>
    <p>
      The FIT reader and writer were written for this site from the published protocol description. The code was
      written with the help of AI coding tools and is covered by automated tests, including checks against real
      device recordings and against a separate open-source decoder. The guides were drafted with AI assistance and
      their platform-specific steps were checked against the official help pages listed at the end of each one.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nobody here claims to have tested every device or every platform. Where something has not been verified, the
      page says so.
    </p>

    <h2>How it is paid for</h2>
    <p>
      The tools are free. The site costs almost nothing to run because your browser does the work. If that changes,
      for instance if advertising or paid extras are added, this page and the <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>
      will say exactly what changed.
    </p>

    {
      site.contactEmail && (
        <>
          <h2>Contact</h2>
          <p>
            Found a file the tools get wrong? Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
            Please describe the problem first instead of attaching the file.
          </p>
        </>
      )
    }
  </article>
</Layout>
